label story_07_complete (The Final Bloom Complete)
[style name="Gameplay"]
"Dianthus Core" (Default): …the Devourer is gone.
"Dianthus Core": For the first time since you found me — bruised and fading in the dark — the hunger is not pressing its mouth against the garden wall. I can feel the silence. It is not empty. It is peace.
"Dianthus Core": Every shard you gathered, every weapon you forged with shaking hands, every root you planted in soil you were afraid to touch — all of it became part of this bloom. All of it mattered.
"Dianthus Core": Rest now, little alchemist. The endless night has broken, and the Dianthus light belongs to the dawn. You gave it back to us.
[signal arg="story_complete:the_final_bloom"]
[end_timeline]
